      "title": "[Advisory] Microsoft Power Pages misconfiguration exposes sensitive data",
      "content": "\n##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\n- Unauthenticated attackers can access and exfiltrate sensitive personal, financial, and organizational data from public-facing portals via exposed Dataverse tables.  \n- **Current exploitation status**: Actively Exploited\n\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\n- Microsoft Power Pages  \n- Microsoft Power Apps Portals\n\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\n- **Prerequisites:** Public-facing Power Pages portal with \"Anonymous Users\" web role granted read permissions on sensitive Dataverse tables.  \n- **Available Mitigations:**\n    - Microsoft provides configuration guidance to disable anonymous access and restrict table permissions.  \n    - **Temporary:** Disable anonymous access, review table permissions, disable unnecessary Web API and OData feeds, and validate endpoint restrictions using an unauthenticated browser session.\n\n##### REFERENCES:\nPrimary:  \n- Source Advisory: [https://venarix.com/blog/exfilsquad-targets-misconfigured-microsoft-power-pages-portals](https://venarix.com/blog/exfilsquad-targets-misconfigured-microsoft-power-pages-portals)\n- Mitigation Guidance: [https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-pages/security/disable-anonymous-access](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-pages/security/disable-anonymous-access)\n\n\n*Timestamp of the Information: 04.08.2026, 10:25*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "A misconfiguration in Microsoft Power Pages portals has been actively exploited to exfiltrate sensitive data stored in Microsoft Dataverse. Microsoft Power Pages portals are vulnerable when the \"Anonymous Users\" web role is granted excessive read permissions on Dataverse tables, making the data publicly accessible to unauthenticated users.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12823"
    },
