      "title": "[Advisory] IBM WebSphere Application Server: Multiple Critical Vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-14446 & CVE-2026-14512)",
      "content": "##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\r\n- Successful exploitation allows unauthenticated remote attackers to bypass authentication, escalate privileges, and execute arbitrary code, leading to full system compromise.\r\n- **Current exploitation status**: UNKNOWN\r\n\r\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\r\n- IBM WebSphere Application Server\r\nFor specific versions, please check the references.\r\n\r\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\r\n- **Prerequisites:** Network access to the application server or administrative console.\r\n- **Available Mitigations:**\r\n    - Vendor interim fixes (APARs) are available immediately.\r\n    - Official patches are scheduled for release in the third quarter.\r\n\r\n##### CVEs IN THIS ADVISORY:\r\n- CVE-2026-14446 CVSS 3.1: 9.8 (CRITICAL) - Privilege escalation in the administrative console\r\n- CVE-2026-14512 CVSS 3.1: 9.8 (CRITICAL) - Pre-authentication unsafe deserialization leading to RCE\r\n- CVE-2026-14528 CVSS 3.1: 7.4 (HIGH) - Sensitive information exposure via logs\r\n\r\n##### REFERENCES:\r\nPrimary:\r\n- Vendor Advisory for CVE-2026-14446: https://www.ibm.com/support/pages/node/7281631\r\n- Vendor Advisory for CVE-2026-14512 & CVE-2026-14528: https://www.ibm.com/support/pages/node/7281649\r\n\r\nSupporting:\r\n- News Coverage: https://www.heise.de/news/IBM-WebSphere-Application-Server-Sicherheitsproblem-in-Admin-Konsole-geloest-11386356.html\r\n\r\n*Timestamp of the Information: 31.07.2026, 14:05*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "Multiple security vulnerabilities have been identified in IBM WebSphere Application Server. The most critical flaws reside in the administrative console and deserialization processes, potentially allowing unauthorized users to gain elevated privileges, bypass authentication, and execute arbitrary code. ",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12821"
    },
