      "title": "[Advisory] SolarWinds Web Help Desk: Critical Authentication Bypass (CVE-2026-28323)",
      "content": "##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\r\n- Successful exploitation allows unauthenticated attackers to bypass authentication and gain unauthorized access to the application.\r\n- **Current exploitation status**: UNKNOWN\r\n\r\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\r\n- SolarWinds Web Help Desk\r\n- For specific versions, please check the references.\r\n\r\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\r\n- **Prerequisites:** For the authentication bypass, the SAML 2.0 authentication method must be enabled on the target system.\r\n- **Impact Details:** Exploiting the vulnerability allows unauthenticated attackers to bypass authentication. \r\n- **Available Mitigations:**\r\n    - Vendor patches available\r\n\r\n##### CVEs IN THIS ADVISORY:\r\n- CVE-2026-28323 CVSS3.1: 9.8 (CRITICAL) - SAML authentication bypass allowing unauthorized access\r\n\r\n##### REFERENCES:\r\nPrimary:\r\n- Vendor Advisory: https://www.solarwinds.com/trust-center/security-advisories/cve-2026-28323\r\n- Vendor Release Notes: https://documentation.solarwinds.com/en/success_center/whd/content/release_notes/whd_2026-2-1_release_notes.htm\r\n\r\nSupporting:\r\n- News Coverage: https://www.heise.de/news/SolarWinds-Web-Help-Desk-Update-bessert-umgehbare-Authentifizierung-aus-11388191.html\r\n\r\n*Timestamp of the Information: 31.07.2026, 13:25*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "A critical security vulnerability has been disclosed in SolarWinds Web Help Desk that allows remote attackers to bypass SAML authentication and gain unauthorized access to the application.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12820"
    },
