      "title": "[Advisory] Cisco Secure FMC: Hard-coded Password Exploited in Zero-Day Attacks (CVE-2026-20316)",
      "content": "##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\n- Successful exploitation allows attackers to gain unauthorized access to affected devices via hard-coded static credentials, potentially leading to full compromise of the firewall management platform.\n- **Current exploitation status**: Actively Exploited\n\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\n- Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC)\n\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\n- **Attack Chain:** CVE-2026-20316 leverages a hard-coded/static password embedded in Cisco Secure FMC, enabling attackers to authenticate and gain unauthorized access.\n- **Prerequisites:** Network access to the affected FMC appliance.\n- **Available Mitigations:**\n    - Vendor patches available\n\n##### CVEs IN THIS ADVISORY:\n- CVE-2026-20316 - Use of hard-coded password in Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center enabling unauthorized access (actively exploited)\n\n##### REFERENCES:\nPrimary:\n- Source Advisory: https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-fmc-static-cred-BET3Cjh\n\n\nSupporting:\n- https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cisco-warns-of-fmc-static-credential-flaw-exploited-in-zero-day-attacks/\n\n- Additional Sources: https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2026/07/29/cisa-adds-one-known-exploited-vulnerability-catalog (CISA KEV Catalog addition confirming active exploitation)\n\n*Timestamp of the Information: 30.07.2026, 07:40*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "A critical security vulnerability has been disclosed in Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC) that involves the use of a hard-coded static password. This flaw is being actively exploited in zero-day attacks, potentially allowing attackers to gain unauthorized access to affected appliances.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12816"
    },
