      "title": "[Advisory] VMware: Multiple Critical Vulnerabilities in ESX, vCenter, Workstation and Fusion (VMSA-2026-0006)",
      "content": "##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\r\n- Successful exploitation could allow unauthenticated attackers to bypass identity controls, execute arbitrary code, or securely escape virtual machines to gain full control over the underlying host infrastructure.\r\n- **Current exploitation status**: UNKNOWN\r\n\r\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\r\n- VMware ESX\r\n- VMware vCenter\r\n- VMware Workstation\r\n- VMware Fusion\r\n- VMware Cloud Foundation\r\n- VMware vSphere Foundation\r\n- VMware Telco Cloud Platform\r\n- For specific versions, please check the references.\r\n\r\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\r\n- **Prerequisites:** Network access to the vCenter server, or local administrative privileges within a VM using the VMXNET3 virtual network adapter.\r\n- **Available Mitigations:**\r\n    - Vendor patches available\r\n\r\n##### CVEs IN THIS ADVISORY:\r\n- CVE-2026-59309 CVSS3.1: 9.8 (CRITICAL) - Authentication bypass in the VMware Directory Service allowing unauthorized system access.\r\n- CVE-2026-59310 CVSS3.1: 9.8 (CRITICAL) - Directory traversal in the Syslog server allowing arbitrary code execution.\r\n- CVE-2026-47876 CVSS3.1: 9.3 (CRITICAL) - Out-of-bounds write in the VMXNET3 virtual network adapter leading to VM escape to the host.\r\n- CVE-2026-41703 CVSS3.1: 7.6 (HIGH) - Out-of-bounds read leading to denial-of-service or information disclosure.\r\n- CVE-2026-41709 CVSS3.1: 2.7 (LOW) - Insufficient logging vulnerability allowing unrecorded administrative actions.\r\n\r\n##### REFERENCES:\r\nPrimary:\r\n- Source Advisory: https://support.broadcom.com/web/ecx/support-content-notification/-/external/content/SecurityAdvisories/0/38017\r\n- Supplemental FAQ: https://github.com/vmware/vcf-security-and-compliance-guidelines/tree/main/security-advisories/vmsa-2026-0006\r\n\r\nSupporting:\r\n- News Coverage: https://www.securityweek.com/critical-vm-escape-vulnerability-patched-in-vmware-esxi/\r\n\r\n*Timestamp of the Information: 29.07.2026, 14:55*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "Broadcom has released security patches addressing multiple vulnerabilities across VMware ESX, vCenter, Workstation, and Fusion. The most severe flaws include a critical virtual machine (VM) escape and an authentication bypass, potentially granting attackers full control over affected host systems and management servers.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12814"
    },
