      "title": "[Advisory] Check Point SmartConsole: Admin Authentication Bypass (CVE-2026-16232)",
      "content": "##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\n- Successful exploitation allows unauthenticated remote attackers to gain full administrative privileges and alter security configurations via network access.\n- **Current exploitation status**: Actively Exploited\n\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\n- Check Point Security Management Server\n- Check Point Multi-Domain Security Management Server (MDS)\n- For specific versions, please check the references.\n\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\n- **Prerequisites:** Internet access to the Management Server IP and unrestricted Trusted Clients (GUI clients) configuration.\n- **Available Mitigations:**\n    - Vendor patches available\n    - **Temporary:** Restrict Trusted Clients to trusted IP addresses and enforce firewall rules to limit management access.\n\n##### CVEs IN THIS ADVISORY:\n- CVE-2026-16232 CVSS3.1: 9.1 (CRITICAL) - Authentication bypass allowing unauthenticated admin login via application tokens\n\n##### REFERENCES:\n\nPrimary:\n- Source Advisory: https://support.checkpoint.com/results/sk/sk185169\n\nSupporting:\n\n- Additional Sources: https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog?field_cve=CVE-2026-16232 (CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities Catalog)\n\n*Timestamp of the Information: 23.07.2026, 08:08*\n\n**Update 29.07.26**\n\n**Current exploitation status:** Actively Exploited, Proof of Concept Available  \n\nRapid7 published a technical analysis and Proof of Concept CVE-2026-16232: \n- technical analysis: https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/ra-check-point-smartconsole-authentication-bypass-technical-analysis-cve-2026-16232/\n- Proof of Concept: https://github.com/sfewer-r7/CVE-2026-16232",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "A critical security vulnerability has been disclosed in Check Point SmartConsole that allows unauthenticated remote attackers to bypass authentication and gain administrative control. By obtaining an application login token, attackers can authenticate with full administrative privileges to apply changes to security policies and configurations.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12793"
    },
    {
