      "title": "Arista VeloCloud Orchestrator: Remote OS Command Injection (CVE-2026-16812)",
      "content": "##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\r\n- Successful exploitation allows unauthenticated remote attackers to execute arbitrary commands and fully compromise the primary orchestrator host and managed edge devices via network access.\r\n- **Current exploitation status**: Actively Exploited\r\n\r\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\r\n- VeloCloud Orchestrator On-Prem (Arista Networks / Broadcom)\r\n- For specific versions, please check the references.\r\n\r\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\r\n- **Prerequisites:** Network access to the VCO web interface. VCO is exposed by default.\r\n- **Impact Details:** Attackers can execute host commands, alter configurations, extract database contents, and potentially pivot to associated managed edge devices.\r\n- **Available Mitigations:**\r\n    - Vendor patches available\r\n    - **Temporary:** Restrict web interface access to trusted administrative networks and block known malicious IPs.\r\n\r\n##### CVEs IN THIS ADVISORY:\r\n- CVE-2026-16812 CVSS4.0: 10.0 (CRITICAL) - OS command injection allowing privileged internal access and host compromise\r\n\r\n##### REFERENCES:\r\nPrimary:\r\n- Source Advisory: https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24364-security-advisory-0144\r\n\r\nSupporting:\r\n- News Coverage: https://thehackernews.com/2026/07/attackers-exploit-arista-velocloud.html\r\n- Additional Sources: https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2026/07/27/cisa-adds-two-known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog\r\n\r\n*Timestamp of the Information: 28.07.2026, 11:14*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "A critical security vulnerability has been identified in Arista Networks' VeloCloud Orchestrator On-Prem that allows unauthorized remote command execution. Attackers have actively exploited this zero-day flaw in the wild to gain access to privileged internal functionality intended only for administrative use. If successfully leveraged, this vulnerability could lead to full compromise of the orchestrator host and the data it manages.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12809"
    },
