      "title": "[Advisory] Fortinet: Fixes multiple vulnerabilities in February 2026 update",
      "content": "##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\n- Successful exploitation allows unauthenticated remote attackers to execute arbitrary code, bypass authentication, or persist on compromised systems via patch circumvention.\n- **Current exploitation status**: UNKNOWN\n\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\n- FortiOS\n- FortiSandbox\n- FortiClientEMS\n- FortiAuthenticator\n- FortiClient for Windows\n- FortiGate\n- For specific versions, please check the references.\n\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\n**CVE-2025-68686** allows bypassing patches for historical flaws (i.e. CVE-2022-42475, CVE-2024-21762) to maintain read-only filesystem access on previously compromised devices.  \n**Prerequisites:** Prior system compromise at the filesystem level (for patch bypass).\n\n**CVE-2025-52436** allows unauthenticated command execution via XSS  \n**Prerequisites:** User intereraction from the victim to trigger the XSS.\n \n\n \n**CVE-2026-21643** (which had a [dedicated CSH Post](https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12362) permits remote code execution via SQL injection.  \n\n**Available Mitigations:**\n- Vendor patches available\n\n\n##### CVEs IN THIS ADVISORY:\n- CVE-2022-42475 CVSS3.1: 9.8 (CRITICAL) - Historical Heap-based buffer overflow in SSL-VPN leading to RCE\n- CVE-2023-27997 CVSS3.1: 9.8 (CRITICAL) - Historical Heap-based buffer overflow in SSL-VPN pre-authentication\n- CVE-2024-21762 CVSS3.1: 9.8 (CRITICAL) - Historical Out-of-bounds write allowing RCE\n- CVE-2026-21643 CVSS3.1: 9.8 (CRITICAL) - SQL Injection in FortiClientEMS allowing unauthenticated RCE\n- CVE-2025-52436 CVSS3.1: 8.8 (HIGH) - XSS in FortiSandbox allowing unauthenticated command execution\n- CVE-2025-68686 CVSS3.1: 5.9 (MEDIUM) - Patch bypass for SSL-VPN allowing persistence on compromised devices\n\n##### REFERENCES:\nPrimary:\n- Source Advisory: https://www.securityweek.com/fortinet-patches-high-severity-vulnerabilities/\n- Vendor Advisory (CVE-2025-68686): https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-25-934\n- Vendor Advisory (CVE-2025-52436): https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-25-093\n- Vendor Advisory (CVE-2026-21643): https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-25-1142\n\n*Timestamp of the Information: 12.02.2026, 08:23*\n\n**Update 28.07.2026**\n\nCISA added CVE-2025-68686 to their Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog.  https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "Fortinet has released security updates addressing multiple high-severity vulnerabilities across its product portfolio. These flaws allow unauthenticated attackers to execute arbitrary commands, bypass authentication mechanisms, and notably circumvent patches for historically exploited SSL-VPN vulnerabilities to maintain persistence.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12371"
    },
