      "title": "[Advisory] Progress MOVEit Transfer: Multiple High Severity Vulnerabilities",
      "content": "\r\n##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\r\n- Successful exploitation could allow attackers to bypass authentication, hijack user sessions, or execute malicious scripts through network access to the application.\r\n- **Current exploitation status**: UNKNOWN\r\n\r\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\r\n- Progress MOVEit Transfer\r\n- For specific versions, please check the references.\r\n\r\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\r\n- **Prerequisites:** Network access to the vulnerable MOVEit Transfer application endpoints or interfaces.\r\n- **Available Mitigations:**\r\n    - Vendor patches available\r\n\r\n##### CVEs IN THIS ADVISORY:\r\n- CVE-2026-10697 CVSS 3.1 (7.5 HIGH) - Improper authentication enforcement\r\n- CVE-2026-15966 CVSS 3.1 (7.5 HIGH) - Permissive cross-domain security policy\r\n- CVE-2026-15967 CVSS 3.1 (7.5 HIGH) - Insufficient session expiration handling\r\n- CVE-2026-15968 CVSS 3.1 (7.1 HIGH) - Cross-site scripting (XSS) via unfiltered input\r\n\r\n##### REFERENCES:\r\nPrimary:\r\n- Source Advisory: https://docs.progress.com/bundle/moveit-transfer-release-notes-2026/page/Fixed-Issues-in-2026.0.3.html\r\n\r\nSupporting:\r\n- News Coverage: https://www.heise.de/news/Sicherheitsupdate-Dateitransferloesung-MOVEit-ist-verwundbar-11379295.html\r\n\r\n*Timestamp of the Information: 28.07.2026, 09:34*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "Several high-severity security vulnerabilities have been identified in the Progress MOVEit Transfer solution that could lead to unauthorized access and potential code execution. These flaws pertain to authentication issues, insufficient session expiration, and cross-site scripting (XSS), which could allow attackers to compromise enterprise file transfer operations and sensitive data.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12808"
    },
