      "files": [],
      "title": "[Advisory] Alibaba Fastjson 1.x : Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution (CVE-2026-16723)",
      "content": "##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\n- Successful exploitation enables unauthenticated remote code execution on vulnerable servers, potentially leading to full system compromise.\n- **Current exploitation status**: Actively Exploited, Proof of Concept Available\n\n\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\n- Alibaba Fastjson 1.2.68 through 1.2.83 (affected versions run in default configuration)\n- Spring Boot applications deployed as executable fat\u2011JARs using an affected Fastjson version  \n\n\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\n- **Prerequisites:** \n - Network access to a target application that parses attacker\u2011controlled JSON via `JSON.parse`, `JSON.parseObject(String)`, or `JSON.parseObject(String, Class)`; \n - Fastjson SafeMode disabled (default); \n- **Available Mitigations:**\n    - No official patched Fastjson 1.x version exists at the time of writing, affected parties should migrate to Fastjson2.\n    - **Temporary:** Enable SafeMode via `-Dfastjson.parser.safeMode=true` \n\n##### CVEs IN THIS ADVISORY:\n- CVE-2026-16723 CVSS3.1: 9.0 (CRITICAL) \u2013 Unauthenticated RCE in Fastjson 1.x default configuration when running inside a Spring Boot fat\u2011JAR.\n\n##### REFERENCES:\nPrimary:\n- Source Advisory: https://github.com/alibaba/fastjson2/wiki/Security-Advisory:-Remote-Code-Execution-in-fastjson-1.2.68%E2%80%931.2.83\n- Technical Analysis (PoC): https://fearsoff.org/research/fastjson-1-2-83-rce \n\nSupporting:\n\n- Additional Sources:  \n  - https://threatbook.io/blog/fastjson-rce-1.2.83-active-exploitation-detected-detection-mitigation  \n  - https://www.imperva.com/blog/imperva-customers-protected-against-cve-2026-16723-critical-fastjson-1-x-zero-day-rce/\n- News Coverage: https://thehackernews.com/2026/07/fastjson-1x-rce-vulnerability-targeted.html    \n\n*Timestamp of the Information: 27.07.2026, 13:46*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "A remote code execution vulnerability has been disclosed in Alibaba\u2019s Fastjson 1.2.68 through 1.2.83. The flaw, exploitable under default configurations in Spring Boot fat\u2011JAR deployments, allows unauthenticated attackers to execute arbitrary code via crafted JSON requests without requiring AutoType or classpath gadgets.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12805"
    },
    {
      "id": 12804,
