      "title": "[Advisory] Zimbra Classic Web Client: Information Disclosure via Specially Crafted Email ",
      "content": "##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\n- Successful exploitation allows unauthenticated remote attackers to access session data, account settings, and mailbox contents when a victim opens a malicious email.\n- **Current exploitation status**: UNKNOWN\n\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\n- Zimbra Collaboration Suite (ZCS) Classic Web Client\n- For specific versions, please check the references.\n\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\n- **Prerequisites:** User must open a specially crafted malicious email sent by the attacker with the Classic Web Client.\n- **Available Mitigations:**\n    - Vendor patches available\n\n##### REFERENCES:\n\nPrimary:\n- Source Advisory: https://blog.zimbra.com/2026/07/patch-release-update-zimbra-10-1-19/\n\nSupporting:\n- News Coverage: https://www.heise.de/news/Zimbra-Collaboration-Suite-Kritische-Luecke-macht-Classic-Web-Client-angreifbar-11356522.html\n\n*Timestamp of the Information: 10.07.2026, 14:35*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "A critical security vulnerability has been disclosed in Zimbra Collaboration Suite's Classic Web Client. The vulnerability allows specialized email parsing flaws to execute malicious code upon viewing an email. Organizations utilizing the affected software are urged to patch immediately to protect sensitive mailbox information.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12757"
    },
