      "title": "[Advisory] Oracle: Multiple critical vulnerabilities fixed in July 2026 patch update",
      "content": "\n##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\n- Successful exploitation of these vulnerabilities allows unauthenticated attackers to gain remote code execution, alter database records, or cause denial-of-service conditions via network-based attacks.\n- **Current exploitation status**: UNKNOWN\n\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\n- For specific product list and versions, please check the references.\n\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\n- **Available Mitigations:**\n    - Vendor patches available\n\n\n##### REFERENCES:\n\nPrimary:\n- Source Advisory: [https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpujul2026.html](https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpujul2026.html)\n\n*Timestamp of the Information: 22.07.2026, 10:52*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "Oracle released its July patch update, addressing a record-breaking number of security vulnerabilities across multiple product lines. Many of these flaws are remotely exploitable without authentication, potentially allowing attackers to gain full control of affected systems. Administrators are strongly urged to apply the updates immediately to prevent unauthorized access and compromise of critical business infrastructure.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12786"
    },
    {
