      "title": "[Advisory] SolarWinds Serv-U: Multiple Critical Security Vulnerabilities in July 2026 update",
      "content": "##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\n- Successful exploitation allows authenticated attackers to escalate privileges to system administrator and execute arbitrary code with root privileges via network access.\n- **Current exploitation status**: UNKNOWN\n\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\n- SolarWinds Serv-U\n- For specific versions, please check the references.\n\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\n- **Prerequisites:** Network access to the deployment and valid user authentication with high privileges.\n- **Available Mitigations:**\n    - Vendor patches available\n\n##### CVEs IN THIS ADVISORY:\n- CVE-2026-28302 CVSS3.1: 9.1 (CRITICAL) - IDOR leading to privilege escalation and remote code execution as root for group administrators.\n- CVE-2026-28304 CVSS3.1: 9.1 (CRITICAL) - Remote code execution vulnerability allowing arbitrary code execution as root.\n- CVE-2026-28314 CVSS3.1: 9.1 (CRITICAL) - IDOR leading to arbitrary account takeover for authenticated users.\n- CVE-2026-28316 CVSS3.1: 9.1 (CRITICAL) - IDOR allowing domain administrators to escalate privileges to system administrator with root execution.\n- CVE-2026-28317 CVSS3.1: 9.1 (CRITICAL) - IDOR requiring domain administrator access that leads to privilege escalation.\n- CVE-2026-28321 CVSS3.1: 9.1 (CRITICAL) - Broken access control allowing domain administrators to read/write arbitrary files and execute root commands.\n- CVE-2026-28315 CVSS3.1: 6.2 (MEDIUM) - Stored cross-site scripting (XSS) potentially leading to session hijacking or admin information disclosure.\n\n##### REFERENCES:\n\nPrimary:\n- Source Advisory: [SolarWinds Serv-U 2026.3 Release Notes](https://documentation.solarwinds.com/en/success_center/servu/content/release_notes/servu_2026-3_release_notes.htm)\n\nSupporting:\n- Additional Sources: [SolarWinds CVE-2026-28302 Security Advisory](https://www.solarwinds.com/trust-center/security-advisories/CVE-2026-28302)\n- Additional Sources: [SolarWinds CVE-2026-28304 Security Advisory](https://www.solarwinds.com/trust-center/security-advisories/CVE-2026-28304)\n- Additional Sources: [SolarWinds CVE-2026-28314 Security Advisory](https://www.solarwinds.com/trust-center/security-advisories/CVE-2026-28314)\n- Additional Sources: [SolarWinds CVE-2026-28315 Security Advisory](https://www.solarwinds.com/trust-center/security-advisories/CVE-2026-28315)\n- Additional Sources: [SolarWinds CVE-2026-28316 Security Advisory](https://www.solarwinds.com/trust-center/security-advisories/CVE-2026-28316)\n- Additional Sources: [SolarWinds CVE-2026-28317 Security Advisory](https://www.solarwinds.com/trust-center/security-advisories/CVE-2026-28317)\n- Additional Sources: [SolarWinds CVE-2026-28321 Security Advisory](https://www.solarwinds.com/trust-center/security-advisories/CVE-2026-28321)\n- News Coverage: [Heise Online Security News (German)](https://www.heise.de/news/Datentransfersoftware-Serv-U-hat-15-kritische-Sicherheitsluecken-11373098.html)\n\n*Timestamp of the Information: 22.07.2026, 10:36*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "SolarWinds addressed multiple critical vulnerabilities in file transfer software Serv-U as part of its July 2026 update. Successful exploitation of these flaws could allow authenticated users to bypass access controls, escalate privileges, and execute arbitrary code. Users are strongly recommended to apply the vendor updates immediately to secure their deployments.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12785"
    },
