      "title": "[Advisory] Veeam Appliances: Local Privilege Escalation to Root (CVE-2026-56844)",
      "content": "##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\n- Successful exploitation allows local authenticated attackers to escalate their privileges to root level, gaining full system control of the underlying operating system.\n- **Current exploitation status**: UNKNOWN\n\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\n- Veeam Software Appliance (Veeam)\n- Veeam Infrastructure Appliance (Veeam)\n- For specific versions, please check the references.\n\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\n- **Prerequisites:** Local authenticated access to the affected appliance.\n- **Available Mitigations:**\n    - Vendor patches are available\n\n##### CVEs IN THIS ADVISORY:\n- CVE-2026-56844 CVSS4.0: 8.4 (HIGH) - A vulnerability in the Veeam Updater component allowing local users to elevate privileges and gain root-level access.\n\n##### REFERENCES:\n\nPrimary:\n- Source Advisory: https://www.veeam.com/kb4879\n\nSupporting:\n- News Coverage: https://www.heise.de/news/Backupsoftware-Veeam-Updater-ermoeglicht-Rechteausweitung-11372985.html\n- News Coverage: https://www.heise.de/en/news/Backup-software-Veeam-Updater-allows-privilege-escalation-11373057.html\n\n*Timestamp of the Information: 22.07.2026, 10:17*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "A security vulnerability has been disclosed in the Veeam Updater component of Veeam Software Appliance and Veeam Infrastructure Appliance. The flaw allows local users with limited privileges to elevate their access, granting root-level permissions on the underlying Linux-based operating system. While Windows-based installations are not directly affected, remote components running on the Linux appliances remain vulnerable.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12784"
    },
