      "title": "[Advisory] Zimbra: Multiple Vulnerabilities Patched in  v 10.1.20",
      "content": "##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\n- **Current exploitation status**: UNKNOWN\n\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\n- Zimbra Collaboration Suite\n- For specific versions, please check the references.\n\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\n- **Available Mitigations:**\n    - Vendor patches are available.\n\n\n##### REFERENCES:\nPrimary:\n- Source Advisory: https://blog.zimbra.com/2026/07/patch-release-update-zimbra-10-1-20/\n\n*Timestamp of the Information: 21.07.2026, 13:09*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "A set of security vulnerabilities has been disclosed in Zimbra Collaboration Suite that could allow malicious actors to compromise email servers. These flaws include a critical command injection bug in the SNMP monitoring component and several cross-site scripting (XSS) issues in the Classic Web Client.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12782"
    },
