      "title": "[Advisory] ServiceNow AI Platform: Remote Code Execution (CVE-2026-6875)",
      "content": "\n##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\n- Successful exploitation allows an unauthenticated attacker, in certain circumstances, to execute arbitrary code within the ServiceNow platform via network access\n- **Current exploitation status**: Actively exploited\n\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\n- ServiceNow AI Platform (hosted and self-hosted instances)\n- For specific versions, please check the references.\n\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\n- **Prerequisites:** Network access to the ServiceNow platform; certain specific circumstances required for unauthenticated exploitation\n- **Available Mitigations:**\n    - Vendor patches available\n\n##### CVEs IN THIS ADVISORY:\n- CVE-2026-6875 CVSS 9.5 (CRITICAL) - Sandbox escape in ServiceNow AI Platform leading to remote code execution\n\n##### REFERENCES:\nPrimary:\n- Vendor Advisory: https://support.servicenow.com/kb?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=KB3137947\n\nSupporting:\n- News coverage (claims of active exploitation): https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/critical-servicenow-code-execution-flaw-now-exploited-in-attacks/\n\n*Timestamp of the Information: 20.07.2026, 13:55*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "A Remote Code Execution vulnerability has been disclosed in ServiceNow that could allow an unauthenticated attacker to execute arbitrary code within the ServiceNow platform. The vulnerability affects the ServiceNow AI platform and has been addressed through security updates for hosted and self-hosted instances.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12778"
    },
    {
