      "files": [],
      "title": "[Advisory] WordPress Core: Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution (CVE-2026-63030, CVE-2026-60137)",
      "content": "##### SEVERITY AND IMPACT:\n- Successful exploitation allows unauthenticated attackers to achieve complete site compromise and execute arbitrary code via malicious network requests.\n- **Current exploitation status**: Actively Exploited, Proof of Concept Available\n\n##### AFFECTED PRODUCTS:\n- WordPress Core\n- For specific versions, please check the references.\n\n##### VULNERABILITY DETAILS:\n- **Prerequisites:** No authentication or plugins required; stock WordPress installation where persistent object cache (such as Redis or Memcached) is not configured.\n- **Available Mitigations:**\n    - Vendor patches available\n    - **Temporary:** Disable anonymous REST API access or block `/wp-json/batch/v1` and `?rest_route=/batch/v1` requests at the WAF level.\n\n##### CVEs IN THIS ADVISORY:\n- CVE-2026-60137 CVSS3.1: 9.1 (CRITICAL) - SQL injection in WP_Query parameter in WordPress Core\n- CVE-2026-63030 CVSS3.1: 7.5 (HIGH) - REST API batch-route confusion in WordPress Core leading to unauthenticated access\n\n##### REFERENCES:\n\nPrimary:\n- Source Advisory: https://slcyber.io/research-center/wp2shell-pre-authentication-rce-in-wordpress-core\n\nSupporting:\n- Technical Analysis: https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-cve-2026-63030-wp2shell-a-critical-remote-code-execution-vulnerability-in-wordpress-core\n- News Coverage: https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/wordpress-core-wp2shell-rce-flaws-get-public-exploits-patch-now/ (Mention of PoC and active exploitation)\n\n*Timestamp of the Information: 20.07.2026, 08:14*",
      "publicationStatus": "Open",
      "summary": "A critical security vulnerability chain dubbed \"wp2shell\" has been disclosed in WordPress Core, potentially allowing unauthenticated attackers to execute malicious code on affected sites. By abusing a route-confusion vulnerability alongside a SQL injection flaw, remote attackers can bypass authorization controls entirely without any user interaction. This vulnerability affects default, stock installations of WordPress that lack specific caching configurations.",
      "citation_url": "https://security-hub.ncsc.admin.ch/#/posts/12771"
    },
    {
      "id": 12764,
      "tlpStatus": "Clear",
